window.products.push({"id":120491,"name":"GE WB21X10148 Thermostat AP4344046 WB20X10020 WB27X10788 Durable PVM9179SF2SS JNM3151RF1SS JNM1541DM1CC PVM1790DR1WW JVM1790BK01 JVM1540SM2SS PSB1201N","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":14.95,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61R1TsuMn6L._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"💡 Wb21x10148 Thermostat - A high-quality exact equivalent for part numbers AP4344046, 1473831, AH2321365, EA2321365, PS2321365, WB20X10020, WB27X10788. Durable Wb21x10148 Microwave Thermostat Replacement is compatible with General Electric appliances. The Ge Wb21x10148 Microwave Thermostat is responsible for regulating the temperature inside the oven cavity to ensure that it stays within a specific range. Thermal Fuse fits hundreds of models and can be installed in a few minutes. 🔧 DIY eTips Included - Not sure how to replace the part? Helpful information can be found on the page below. Scroll down to get more repair tips. Acquire valuable skills during the DIY repair project. Wb21x10148 Thermostat for Ge Microwaves will help if your appliance doesn't turn on. Unplug your appliance and wear work gloves to protect your hands during the replacement. 💡 The Wb21x10148 Part is a safety component that helps prevent the oven from overheating. It is designed to open and interrupt the electrical circuit to the heating element when the temperature inside the oven reaches a certain level. When the temperature drops below this threshold, the thermostat closes the circuit again, allowing the heating element to resume operation. Thermostat meets or exceeds all manufacturer specifications. We provide a lifetime warranty and guarantee 100% money back. 💡 Replacing the WB21X10148 thermostat requires technical knowledge and basic tools. The process generally involves disconnecting the power supply, removing the back panel of the oven or microwave, locating the thermostat, disconnecting the wires, and removing the old thermostat. The new thermostat can then be installed in its place, and the wires reconnected before reassembling the oven or microwave. 💡 Is it possible to bypass the thermostat? It is not recommended to bypass the thermostat in your range or microwave, as this can compromise the safety of the appliance and pose a fire hazard. The thermostat is a critical safety component designed to prevent the oven or microwave from overheating and causing damage or injury. Attempting to bypass the thermostat can cause the heating element to stay on indefinitely, which can cause the oven or microwave to overheat and potentially start a fire.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61R1TsuMn6L._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PartsBroz","source_asin":"B088TWN65Q","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-120491","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B088TWN65Q","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B088TWN65Q","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
